# ===========================================================================
# Construction Portal — frontend build configuration template
#
# Copy to .env for local work:   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored; this file is the tracked template.
# ===========================================================================
#
# Read by Vite at BUILD time, not at runtime. Every VITE_-prefixed variable
# is substituted into the bundle as a literal string, which means:
#
#   * changing one requires a rebuild, not just a restart;
#   * the value ends up in public JavaScript that anyone can read.
#
# NEVER put a secret here. No service-role key, no database password, no
# SMTP credential. Those belong in backend/.env, which never reaches the
# browser.
# ===========================================================================

# Base URL every API request is built on, including the /api prefix.
# Read once in src/api/axiosClient.js, which falls back to
# http://127.0.0.1:5051/api when this is unset.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ON VERCEL THIS MUST BE SET IN THE DASHBOARD.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frontend/.env is gitignored, so it is not in the repository Vercel builds
# from. If the variable is missing there, the build silently falls back to
# http://127.0.0.1:5051/api and the deployed app calls the visitor's own
# machine. The symptom is a Content-Security-Policy error on every request,
# because `upgrade-insecure-requests` in vercel.json rewrites that http URL
# to https and no connect-src entry matches it.
#
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables → add for Production,
# then redeploy. A rebuild is required; a redeploy of the existing build
# keeps the old baked-in value.
#
# Three things have to agree, or requests are blocked before they are sent:
#   1. this value
#   2. connect-src in frontend/vercel.json
#   3. CORS_ORIGINS on the backend (which lists the FRONTEND origin)
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5051/api
